1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Difahamkan berasal dari Pulau Langga Puri
2 CONT (Pulau Jawa)==============
2 CONT ''''''There are many corrections needed here,the family trees are faulty.Brawijaya V is the 5th King of Majapahit and his ancestor Raden Wijaya is the 1st King of Majapahit.The Sarawakian geneology of Dato Merpati need to update v
2 CONC ia research & archaeological remains''''''.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''''Is it true that King Sanjaya of the Medang kingdom and King Raden Wijaya of the Majapahit kingdom were descendants of the Sunda kingdom?''''
2 CONT
2 CONT Quora : by  Hunter Eyes (nick name)
2 CONT
2 CONT ''''''Objections to the Wangsakerta Manuscript and the Rajya Rajya Library in Bumi Nusantara.''''''
2 CONT
2 CONT Nararya Sanggramawijaya (Dyah Wijaya) in the Balawi inscription of 1305 declared himself a member of the Rajasa dynasty.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the Nagarakretagama Manuscript, Dyah Wijaya was the son of Dyah Lembu Tal, the son of Narasinghamurti. Meanwhile, according to Pararaton, Narasinghamurti alias Mahisa Campaka is the son of Mahisa Wonga Teleng, the son
2 CONC  of Ken Arok, the founder of the Rajasa Dynasty.
2 CONT
2 CONT ["Dyah Wijaya, son of Dyah Lembu Tal, son of Narasinghamurti alias Mahisa Campaka, son of Mahisa Wonga Teleng, son of Ken Arok, king of Singsari, founder of the Rajasa dynasty. Dyah Wijaya was the first king of Majapahit, son-in-l
2 CONC aw of Kertanegara, the last king of Singasari"]
2 CONT
2 CONT With the existence of Nagarakretagama, which is the primary source for UNESCO's "The Memory of the World Register for Asia/Pacific," which states that Dyah Lembu Tal was a man, the son of Narasinghamurti. (This manuscript praises 
2 CONC Dyah Lembu Tal as a brave young officer and was the father of Dyah Wijaya), so it can be confirmed that Nararya Sanggramawijaya alias Dyah Wijaya is of Singasari (Javanese) blood, not a mixture of Singasari (Mother's side) and Sun
2 CONC danese (Mother's side). Father)
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the Nagarakretagama Manuscript, Dyah Lembu Tal was a man and not a woman. Dyah Lembu Tal is the father of Nararya Sanggramawijaya (Dyah Wijaya) who also comes from Singhasari, not Sundanese.
2 CONT
2 CONT Meanwhile, according to the Rajya Rajya i Bhumi Nusantara Library written by Prince Wangsakerta from the Sultanate of Cirebon, Dyah Lembu Tal is described as a woman.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Nagarakretagama Manuscript is a literary book written by Mpu Prapanca around 1350 - 1389 AD, telling the history of the Majapahit Kingdom. The book written on palm leaves was registered in "The Memory of the World Regional Reg
2 CONC ister for Asia/Pacific" as an intangible World Heritage by UNESCO on June 21 2013.
2 CONT
2 CONT Girindra's book also interprets or supports Professor Slamet Muljana's interpretation regarding the origin of Dyah Lembu Tal as a male character, not a female.
2 CONT
2 CONT That Dyah Lembu Tal was the son of Narasingamurti who later gave birth to Nararya Sanggramawijaya (Dyah Wijaya) and Arya Bangah (Mpu Tilam).
2 CONT
2 CONT A year after reigning in Panjalu Daha, Narashingamurti married and from the empress gave birth to a son named Dyah Lembu Tal who was born around 1252 AD. Later Dyah Lembu Tal, from an empress, gave birth to Nararya Sanggramawijaya
2 CONC  (Dyah Wijaya), the founder and first king of the Majapahit Kingdom. [Girindra p. 82]
2 CONT
2 CONT Dyah Lembu Tal's relationship with Sundanese royal blood is probably from the second empress. From the first empress Dyah Lembu Tal descended Nararya Sanggramawijaya (Dyah Wijaya), while from the second wife from the Sunda kingdom
2 CONC  derived Arya Bangah (Mpu Tilam). After coming to Majapahit, Arya Bangah, also known as Mpu Tilam, was appointed Patih Daha to replace Mpu Sora who died in 1300 AD. [Girindra p.84]
2 CONT
2 CONT In conclusion:
2 CONT
2 CONT Among these manuscripts, the validity of the Nagarakretagama can be confirmed because this manuscript was written in 1365 AD, only 56 years after the death of Nararya Singgramawijaya (Dyah Wijaya).
2 CONT
2 CONT Meanwhile, the Wangsakerta manuscript, which consists of Pustaka Rajya Rajya i Bhumi Nusantara, written by Prince Wangsakerta from the Cirebon Sultanate, which was compiled from 1677 to 1685 AD, cannot be confirmed.
2 CONT
2 CONT The news in the Nagarakretagama Manuscript is also strengthened by the Balawi inscription which was published directly by Dyah Wijaya himself in 1305 AD.
2 CONT
2 CONT In this inscription, Nararya Sanggramawijaya (Dyah Wijaya) claims to be an original member of the Wangsa Rajasa, namely the dynasty which according to the Pararaton Manuscript was founded by Ken Arok, the first king of Singasari.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:
2 CONT
2 CONT https://ajisangkala.id/jenis-kelamin-dyah-lembu-tal-menurut-sumber-prasasti/
2 CONT Book: Girindra: Pararaja Tumapel - Majapahit
