1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''MEDIA-NOTES:'''<br/>
2 CONT '''Before: 008/rp04/tg03 and RP04'''<br/>
2 CONT '''Code : 016/RP05'''<br/>
2 CONT '''Next: 023/RP06'''
2 CONT
2 CONT (penghujung abad 14, selepas tahun 1375)
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Maharaja Ananggawarman was a King of the Kingdom of Pagaruyung who ruled from 1375 until 1417. His kingdom covered West Sumatra and a large part of coastal Sumatra except Acheh that had already been conquered by Samudera Pasai.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1409 the Majapahit Empire under Wikramawardhana, son-in-law to Maharaja Dyah Hayam Wuruk, sent a large invading force to conquer Pagaruyung Kingdom. Maharaja Ananggawarman managed to defeat the invading force at the battle of P
2 CONC adang Sibusuk (located in the present Kabupaten Sijunjung.
2 CONT
2 CONT According to the Minangkabau adat archive (the Tambo), Maharaja Annanggawarman was the son of Maharaja Adityawarman and Puti Reno Jalito. Maharaja Annanggawarman married Puti Reno Dewi and had among his children three princesses: 
2 CONC Puti Panjang Rambuik, Puti Salareh Pinang Masak, and Puti Bongsu. These three princesses would marry with his noblemen and form the nobility of Pagaruyung.
2 CONT
2 CONT Upon his death, the Majapahit influence and the Hindu religion in Pagaruyung went in decline.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Also known as Dewang Beramak Sanggowano
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://id.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ananggawarman
2 CONT
2 CONT Ananggawarman adalah anak dari Adityawarman dan Puti Reno Jalito. Ananggawarman menikah dengan Puti Reno Dewi, dan memiliki tiga orang putri yaitu Puti Panjang Rambuik, Puti Salareh Pinang Masak, dan Puti Bongsu. Ketiga putrinya k
2 CONC emudian menikah dengan para pemuka adat, yang kemudian membentuk kaum bangsawan Pagaruyung
