1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Links to Articles Posted below where Imam Abdol Rakibs' name appears.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.google.com.au/amp/s/toyerfarrath.wordpress.com/2010/02/03/self-empowerment-cape-1844-1848/amp/
2 CONT
2 CONT Fatima (Abader) Alexander - 11/12/2019
2 CONT
2 CONT The third oldest masjid in South Africa is the Nurul Islam Masjid situated in a small lane off Buitengracht Street in Cape Town. It was founded in 1844 by the younger of Tuan Guru’s sons, Imam Abdol Rauf and is situated about 100 
2 CONC meters from the Auwal Masjid in Dorp Street. It is not known as to what need there was for this masjid to be constructed so close to the Auwal Masjid.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Nurul Islam Masjid was the first to be founded by a congregation which developed out of friendly-ties which existed among a group of students who acquired Islamic education under the guidance ofImam Achmat van Bengalen. 
2 CONT
2 CONT n about 1830, Tuan Guru’s two sons [Abdol Rakiep and Abdol Rauf] together with Badroen and also Achmat van Bengalen’s three sons [Mochamat, Hamien and Saddik] got together and established the Mohammedan Shafee Congregation with Ab
2 CONC dol Rakiep [d 1834] as Imam. At this stage the Congregation did not have their own masjid. However, their dream was realised on February 27, 1844 when they took transfer of a property in Buitengracht Street, and converted the fron
2 CONC t section into a prayer room.
2 CONT
2 CONT The first imam of the Nurul Islam Masjid was Imam Abdol Rauf from 1844-1859, followed by:
2 CONT
2 CONT Imam Hamien [1859-1867], Imam Abdol Rakiep [1867-1905 ], Imam Mogamat [Muhammad] Taleb [1905 1912], Imam Gabebodien [Habib al-Din] Hartley [1912-1939], Sheikh Ismail Ganief [I-Ian3f] [1939-1954], Imam Armien Basadien [1950-1970], 
2 CONC Sheikh Gamiet [Hamid] Gabier [1970-1973], Hadjie Mustapha Basadien [1973-1979], Hadjie Ebrahim Samoudien [d 1979].
